<div class="terminology-note">
  <details>
    <summary>A note on terminology and logo</summary>
    <p>
      This site does not relinquish the name Bitcoin or its established identity following the chain split. Where
      both chains must be identified explicitly, we use <strong>Bitcoin</strong> and <strong>BTC-SHA256</strong>,
      respectively.
    </p>
    <p>
      Bitcoin retains the orange-and-white ₿, with one distinction: we have pivoted the ₿ upright. It preserves
      Bitcoin's visual identity while giving upright its other meaning: adhering to principle—a renewed commitment
      to the purpose that gave rise to Bitcoin.
    </p>
  </details>
</div>
